✅ Institutional Continuation Model (ICM)

The move happens in three mechanical steps:

Impulse  →  Inventory Correction  →  Re-Initiation
              (trap zone)             (entry)


Your entries must occur ONLY in step-3.

1️⃣ Impulse Leg (Initiative Move)

Smart money establishes direction.

Observable facts

Expansion candle

Break of structure (CPR / R3 / S3)

Range > normal volatility

impulse =
    candle_range > 1.3 * atr and
    close > r3            # CALL example


This tells you:

Auction left balance.

2️⃣ Inventory Correction (The Trap)

Institutions DO NOT chase.

They pause price to:

take profit

reload

trap late buyers/sellers

What it looks like

Small pullback candles

Overlapping bodies

EMA test

Momentum cooling

This is exactly what your circled zones show.

pullback =
    low <= ema_fast and
    close > ema_fast and
    range < atr


Key insight:

Pullback must look weak, not aggressive.

3️⃣ Re-Initiation (Institutional Entry)

This is the real trade.

Price resumes auction after absorption.

Confirmation

Strong body candle

Closes away from EMA

Breaks pullback high

reinitiation =
    close > pullback_high and
    (body / range) > 0.6 and
    momentum_ok

✅ Complete Institutional Continuation Logic
CALL SIDE
def institutional_continuation_long(df, ema_fast, r3, atr):

    last = df.iloc[-1]
    prev = df.iloc[-2]

    body = abs(last.close - last.open)
    rng = last.high - last.low

    # ---- Step 1: impulse already happened ----
    impulse_done = df["close"].iloc[-5:].max() > r3

    # ---- Step 2: pullback ----
    pullback = (
        prev.low <= ema_fast and
        prev.close > ema_fast
    )

    # ---- Step 3: re-initiation ----
    reinitiation = (
        last.close > prev.high and
        (body / rng) > 0.6
    )

    if impulse_done and pullback and reinitiation:
        return True

    return False

PUT SIDE (mirror logic)
def institutional_continuation_short(df, ema_fast, s3, atr):

    last = df.iloc[-1]
    prev = df.iloc[-2]

    body = abs(last.close - last.open)
    rng = last.high - last.low

    impulse_done = df["close"].iloc[-5:].min() < s3

    pullback = (
        prev.high >= ema_fast and
        prev.close < ema_fast
    )

    reinitiation = (
        last.close < prev.low and
        (body / rng) > 0.6
    )

    if impulse_done and pullback and reinitiation:
        return True

    return False

✅ Plug Into detect_signal()

Inside continuation section:

