# =======================

Liquidity Sweep + Continuation Model (LSC)

Institutions need liquidity to enter size.

Where is liquidity?

Above obvious highs

Below obvious lows

Around pivot levels traders watch

So price first moves beyond a level, triggers stops, then returns back, then trends.

Market Microstructure Sequence
1️⃣ Approach Level (R3 / S3)
2️⃣ Sweep Liquidity (wick beyond level)
3️⃣ Acceptance Back Inside
4️⃣ Expansion Move ← ENTRY HERE


Your circled candles are step-4.

Step 1 — Detect Liquidity Sweep
CALL setup (bullish continuation)

Price dips below support briefly.

def liquidity_sweep_long(last, level, atr):
    wick_size = level - last.low

    return (
        last.low < level and                # swept below
        last.close > level and              # reclaimed level
        wick_size > 0.15 * atr              # meaningful sweep
    )

PUT setup (bearish continuation)
def liquidity_sweep_short(last, level, atr):
    wick_size = last.high - level

    return (
        last.high > level and
        last.close < level and
        wick_size > 0.15 * atr
    )

Step 2 — Absorption Filter (VERY IMPORTANT)

We must avoid V-reversal traps.

Institutional absorption shows:

small body candle

long rejection wick

low momentum

def absorption_candle(candle):
    body = abs(candle.close - candle.open)
    rng  = candle.high - candle.low

    return (body / rng) < 0.4

Step 3 — Continuation Trigger

Next candle must show initiative.

def continuation_trigger(curr, prev):
    body = abs(curr.close - curr.open)
    rng  = curr.high - curr.low

    return (
        curr.close > prev.high and
        (body / rng) > 0.6
    )


(reverse for PUT)

✅ Full Institutional LSC Logic
CALL SIDE
def liquidity_continuation_long(df, level, atr):

    if len(df) < 3:
        return False

    sweep = df.iloc[-3]
    absorb = df.iloc[-2]
    trigger = df.iloc[-1]

    if not liquidity_sweep_long(sweep, level, atr):
        return False

    if not absorption_candle(absorb):
        return False

    if continuation_trigger(trigger, absorb):
        return True

    return False

PUT SIDE
def liquidity_continuation_short(df, level, atr):

    if len(df) < 3:
        return False

    sweep = df.iloc[-3]
    absorb = df.iloc[-2]
    trigger = df.iloc[-1]

    if not liquidity_sweep_short(sweep, level, atr):
        return False

    if not absorption_candle(absorb):
        return False

    body = abs(trigger.close - trigger.open)
    rng  = trigger.high - trigger.low

    if trigger.close < absorb.low and (body / rng) > 0.6:
        return True

    return False


Integrate Inside detect_signal()

Place BEFORE normal breakout logic:

# ---- Liquidity Sweep Continuation ----

if liquidity_continuation_long(candles_3m, r3, atr) and call_ok:
    return "CALL", "LIQUIDITY_CONTINUATION"

if liquidity_continuation_short(candles_3m, s3, atr) and put_ok:
    return "PUT", "LIQUIDITY_CONTINUATION"

Why This Works (Institutional Reality)

Retail breakout logic:

Price breaks → Buy


Institutional logic:

Price breaks → collect stops → reverse briefly → then move


