What is Initial Balance (IB)

Initial Balance = High & Low of first 60 minutes

For your system (3-minute candles):

20 candles = 60 minutes


IB defines:

The fair auction range

Where institutions agreed on price early

The launchpad for expansion moves

Why IB Matters

| Behaviour after IB       | Meaning            |
| ------------------------ | ------------------ |
| Break + Hold outside IB  | Trend day starting |
| Fake break → back inside | Trap / reversal    |
| Stay inside IB           | Range day          |


tep 1 — Globals

Add near your other session variables:

initial_balance = {
    "high": None,
    "low": None,
    "complete": False
}

ib_candles = []

✅ Step 2 — Build Initial Balance

Call this on every 3-minute candle close.

def update_initial_balance(candle):

    global ib_candles, initial_balance

    if initial_balance["complete"]:
        return

    ib_candles.append(candle)

    # first 20 candles = 60 minutes
    if len(ib_candles) < 20:
        return

    initial_balance["high"] = max(c.high for c in ib_candles)
    initial_balance["low"]  = min(c.low  for c in ib_candles)
    initial_balance["complete"] = True

    logging.info(
        f"[INITIAL BALANCE] "
        f"High={initial_balance['high']:.2f} "
        f"Low={initial_balance['low']:.2f}"
    )


Call this exactly where you already detect:

[3M CANDLE CLOSED]

✅ Step 3 — Detect IB Break Type

This becomes a market phase detector.

def detect_ib_behavior(price, atr):

    if not initial_balance["complete"]:
        return "IB_FORMING"

    ib_high = initial_balance["high"]
    ib_low  = initial_balance["low"]

    buffer = 0.15 * atr if atr else 5

    if price > ib_high + buffer:
        return "IB_BREAK_UP"

    if price < ib_low - buffer:
        return "IB_BREAK_DOWN"

    return "IB_INSIDE"

