# ✅ Step 2 — Build Liquidity Levels

Call this once after pivots + IB are known.

```python
def build_liquidity_map(cpr, trad, cam):

    global liquidity_map

    buy_side = [
        trad["R1"],
        trad["R2"],
        cam["R3"],
        cam["R4"],
        initial_balance.get("high"),
        prev_day_high
    ]

    sell_side = [
        trad["S1"],
        trad["S2"],
        cam["S3"],
        cam["S4"],
        initial_balance.get("low"),
        prev_day_low
    ]

    liquidity_map["buy_side"] = [x for x in buy_side if x]
    liquidity_map["sell_side"] = [x for x in sell_side if x]

    logging.info(
        f"[LIQUIDITY MAP] BuyStops={len(buy_side)} "
        f"SellStops={len(sell_side)}"
    )
```

---

# ✅ Step 3 — Detect Liquidity Sweep

This is the institutional event.

A sweep = price trades beyond liquidity but fails acceptance.

```python
def detect_liquidity_sweep(candles):

    if len(candles) < 2:
        return None

    last = candles.iloc[-1]
    prev = candles.iloc[-2]

    # ---- Buy-side sweep (stop hunt above) ----
    for level in liquidity_map["buy_side"]:
        if prev["high"] <= level and last["high"] > level:
            if last["close"] < level:
                liquidity_map["last_sweep"] = ("BUY_SWEEP", level)
                return ("BUY_SWEEP", level)

    # ---- Sell-side sweep ----
    for level in liquidity_map["sell_side"]:
        if prev["low"] >= level and last["low"] < level:
            if last["close"] > level:
                liquidity_map["last_sweep"] = ("SELL_SWEEP", level)
                return ("SELL_SWEEP", level)

    return None
```

---

# ✅ Step 4 — Institutional Interpretation

| Sweep Type | Meaning                       | Trade Bias  |
| ---------- | ----------------------------- | ----------- |
| BUY_SWEEP  | Stops above taken → rejection | SHORT / PUT |
| SELL_SWEEP | Stops below taken → rejection | LONG / CALL |

Because smart money just filled positions.

---

